From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elena Maher <12779416+elenaOnline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:20:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpui: Add live regions, disabled state, synthetic subtrees
 and a11y test windows

Apps built on GPUI's AccessKit integration need a few things it lacks to
serve a screen reader well:

- aria_live: a live region (StatefulInteractiveElement::aria_live). The
  AccessKit adapters announce a live region's value when it appears and
  when it changes (on macOS, NSAccessibilityAnnouncementRequestedNotification),
  which is how an app tells a screen reader user what just happened
  ("Rectangle selected") without moving focus.
- aria_disabled: controls that cannot be used right now are reported as
  such ("dimmed" in VoiceOver) instead of looking pressable.
- A11ySubtreeBuilder::push_node: a synthetic subtree deeper than one
  level (a synthetic text field with its text runs), and
  A11ySubtreeBuilder::set_active_descendant: a custom element that keeps
  keyboard focus itself (a canvas editing text, a list drawn by hand) can
  report one of its synthetic children as the focused item, the
  aria-activedescendant pattern that aria_active_descendant already gives
  real elements. Honored only while the element or an ancestor holds
  focus.
- Test windows emulate the platform adapter: they keep the callbacks
  a11y_init gives them and the tree updates the window sends, and
  Window::simulate_a11y_activation / simulate_a11y_deactivation /
  simulate_a11y_action / take_a11y_tree_updates let tests connect
  assistive technology, read the trees a real adapter would receive and
  perform actions on their nodes, headlessly.
